<title>USA: Union Pacific ups estimated benefits of deal.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific ups estimated benefits of deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Corp said on Thursday that it revised its estimate of operating income benefits it expects to achieve from its merger with Southern Pacific Rail Corp to $820 million by 2001, as compared to earlier estimates of $612 million.</p>
<p>Union Pacific said it would implement the Southern Pacific merger in 1997.</p>
<p>-- ((New York newsdesk 212-859-1611))</p>
</text>
